WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.401
Now to a CNN exclusive.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:04.471
Ukraine has a network of secret agents

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.406
working inside Russia

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.742
and helping to sabotage Russian forces.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.043
That is according to U.S.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.277
intelligence services.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.212
And we're also told

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.346
that Ukraine is arming

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.181
these agents with drones.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:15.482
U.S.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.416
officials believe

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.451
these pro-Ukrainian agents inside

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.587
Russia may have been behind

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.323
this drone attack in Moscow earlier

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.524
last month.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.658
CNN's Natasha Bertrand.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.693
Joins us now

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.528
with this exclusive reporting.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.330
First of all, great job on the reporting.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.164
Second of all,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.733
what do we know about these cells

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.835
that are set up to sabotage Russia?

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.271
Yes.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.305
So what we're learning from U.S.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:39.873
officials

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.908
who describe the intelligence to us is

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.810
that these cells are basically made up

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.745
of pro-Ukrainian sympathizers,

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.813
as well as agents

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.715
who are well trained in this style

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.682
of warfare.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.517
And what we're told

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.851
is that these attacks

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.653
really have become a lot more brazen.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.554
Over the last month.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.955
There have been a steady drumbeat

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.924
of strikes against Russian targets

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.625
over the last year,

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.659
including including fuel

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.694
depots, railways, pipelines.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.863
But since that May 3rd strike

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.765
on the Kremlin, that drone strike, U.S.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.800
officials have really noticed

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.700
an uptick here.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.635
And they do attribute

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.302
that drone strike

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.671
to these pro-Ukrainian partizans

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.406
who are working for

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.040
the Ukrainians

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.742
to carry out these strikes inside Russia.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.443
It is unclear

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.911
whether all of the drone strikes

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.445
that we have seen

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.712
over the course of the last

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.280
several weeks

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.114
can be attributed

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:21.815
to that,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.850
those sabotage cells inside Ukraine.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.351
But it's also really interesting

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.319
because we are told

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:26.686
that they are

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.855
being given drones by the Ukrainians.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.223
And we know that Ukraine

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.792
has a very sophisticated and well-honed

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.861
drone manufacturing industry

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.262
that they are really ramping up.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.831
And so it is unclear

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.833
how they're actually getting those drones

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.533
into Russia.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.267
However, we are told

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:41.801
that there are pretty

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.269
well-practiced smuggling routes

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.238
between Ukraine and Russia

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.440
that may have allowed the Ukrainians

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.575
to give these drones

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.210
to the partizans here.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.278
So it really is an interesting window

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.781
into just how Ukraine is bringing the war

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.150
to Russia directly. Sara.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.917
Natasha Bertrand,

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.285
thank you so much for that reporting.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.920
Appreciate it, John.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.988
All right.
New this morning,

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.889
Russia claims

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.024
it has thwarted what it calls

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.159
a large scale

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.260
Ukrainian offensive

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.028
in the southern Donetsk region.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:09.996
That is in

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.131
was in the eastern

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.565
part of the country there.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.266
The Russian defense

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.168
ministry released video that it says

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.470
shows a skirmish with Ukrainian forces.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.272
Moscow says Ukrainian troops

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.073
tried and failed

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.508
to push through a front line

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.643
area with tanks and armored vehicles.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.577
Ukrainian officials say

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.846
they have no information on the incident.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.014
Ukraine has been signaling

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.083
a major count as offensive for weeks.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.351
But in a new video

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.253
circulated on social media,

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.954
Ukrainian soldiers are urging

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.556
everyone to stay quiet.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:39.259
You can see that, say the soldiers.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.662
CNN's Frederik Pleitgen is in key for us

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.329
this morning.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.030
So, Fred,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.466
the Russians are making sounds now

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.301
that some kind of

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.236
Ukrainian effort has begun.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:50.970
Is this

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.705
could this be the counter offensive

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:56.709
Well, it's very, very

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.677
difficult to say, John.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.945
But certainly you're absolutely right

00:02:58.945 --> 00:02:59.879
that the Russians came out

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.181
actually late last night

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.549
and put out that video

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.249
that you were just showing.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.117
They were just talking about

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:04.651
as well as saying

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.485
if they had thwarted

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.619
a large scale attack,

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.320
as they put it,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.421
by the Ukrainians,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.323
they claim that they took out 16

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.324
Ukrainian tanks,

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.392
also a bunch of infantry

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.359
fighting vehicles

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.527
and a bunch of Ukrainian

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.528
soldiers as well.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.763
I think they were talking about

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.065
around 250 Ukrainian soldiers,

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.632
as you said.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.200
So far,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.634
no information whatsoever

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.069
coming from the Ukrainian side.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:23.670
Quite interesting though,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.171
because earlier today,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.339
in fact,
not long ago,

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.441
another Russian official from that area

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.043
where all this is going on,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.944
he claimed that there was

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.512
another Ukrainian attack

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:33.780
that happened this warning,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.315
this time larger in scale.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.083
And he claims that the Ukrainians

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.484
are trying to advance

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.552
through Russian positions

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.920
and get all the way down

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.522
to the Sea of Azov.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.223
Now, of course,

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:43.556
they are

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.858
very far away from making that happen.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.227
But if they did manage to do that,

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.294
it would be a huge breakthrough

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.229
for the Ukrainians

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.330
because then they could cut off

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:50.797
the land

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.865
corridor that the Russians have

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.601
from Russian territory

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.436
all the way to Crimea again.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:56.936
Right now,

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.172
all this seems to be in the early stages

00:03:59.172 --> 00:03:59.672
if it's something

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.640
that is actually going on.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.174
And of course,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.775
we have that complete radio silence

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.110
there coming from the Ukrainians.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.311
You just showed that ad.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.347
That certainly was something that caused

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.148
a lot of chuckles here in Ukraine

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.650
over this weekend when it was released.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.152
The message of that, by the way, is plans

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.153
love silence.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.923
John plans love silence.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.091
So, Fred, over the last

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.591
several weeks,

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.792
there's been a lot of focus

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:23.396
inside Russia in the Belgorod region,

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.931
which is just north

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.099
of the Ukrainian border,

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:26.499
not far

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.368
from the Ukrainian city of Kharkiv.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.802
What's going on there today?

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.339
That same

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.607
same stuff still going on

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.276
and the Russians still not being able

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.277
to come to terms with it.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:37.677
In fact,

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:38.711
just a couple of minutes ago,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.747
the governor of that region, he came out

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.282
and said that overnight,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:45.785
some 600 projectiles were fired to buy,

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:46.653
as he put it,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.987
from the Ukrainian side

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.122
towards the territory,

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.423
which is around the town of Quebec,

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.257
which is right

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.625
next to the border between

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.693
Ukraine and Russia.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.028
Now, that, of course, includes

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.096
various munitions, can include mortars,

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.231
that can include artillery,

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.365
but also bullets as well.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.366
But certainly there is a lot

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.334
going on there.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.303
And those pro-Russian fighter

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.370
other those those Russian

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.372
fighters, anti-Putin, Russian fighters

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.674
who have been on the ground there,

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.142
they claim that they're still in

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.076
part of that area.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.311
Very difficult to discern.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:11.911
But one of the things

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.246
that certainly seems to be the case

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.348
is that
the Russians are on the back foot.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:15.982
Look, one thing

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:16.983
that is also for certain,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.118
there has been an uptick in activity

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.320
across the region.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.688
Frederik Pleitgen in key for us

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.222
this morning, Fred, to keep us posted.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.023
Meanwhile, the top U.S.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:24.824
military officer

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.559
saying Ukraine is well-prepared

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.827
for a counter-offensive.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.696
General Mark Milley, chairman of the U.S.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.431
Joint Chiefs of Staff,

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:32.732
had an exclusive interview

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.199
with CNN's

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:33.800
or Lehman

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.301
in France ahead of tomorrow's

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.270
79th anniversary of D-Day

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.271
and joins us now

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.139
from Normandy to see

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.007
what you discussed on

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.344
Max, this was

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.211
a wide ranging

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.245
interview that first covered

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.447
why we're here in Normandy.

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:49.515
79 years after the D-Day invasion.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.417
We certainly talked some about that,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.352
his personal feelings

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.153
his professional feelings being here.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.021
He's been here before,

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:55.788
but the significance

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:56.989
it still has for him.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.524
We certainly talked about China

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.992
as well as some of the domestic issues

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.661
in the U.S., the military faces.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:02.128
But of course,

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.162
much of the interview itself

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.364
focused on Ukraine

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:05.732
as we anticipate

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.300
this counteroffensive here and wait

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.735
to see when it begins.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:09.602
He is closely

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:10.503
watched this war

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.304
for the last year

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.538
and a half or so, really

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.741
ever since it began and even before that.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:15.842
Our question to him

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.610
was, are they prepared

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.611
and how do you know

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.213
they will be successful?

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:22.682
He was very careful in his answer here,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:23.983
worrying not to predict

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:25.051
how battles play out

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.253
because of how complex that is to know.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.221
Here's what he had to say.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.891
So I think it's too early to tell

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.393
what outcomes are going to happen.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.360
I think the Ukrainians

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.261
are very well prepared.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.429
As you know very well,

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.497
the United States and other

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.431
allied countries in Europe

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.265
and a really around

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:39.966
the world

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.067
have provided training

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.935
and ammunition and advice,

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:43.970
intelligence, etc.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.671
to the Ukrainians. We're supporting them.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:47.073
They're in a war

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:47.940
that's an essential threat

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.243
for the very survival of Ukraine

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.077
and has greater

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.745
meaning to the rest of the world

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.514
for for Europe,

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:55.915
really for the United States,

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:59.752
but also for the globe

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.522
And speaking about current operations,

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.189
what we're seeing,

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:04.323
what you just talked about, Max,

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:05.725
we also ask about the attacks

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.260
we're seeing inside Russia.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.394
And does that escalate

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.196
or risk the possibility of an escalation

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:10.930
with Russia?

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:11.998
You acknowledge that, yes,

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.366
it could risk an escalation

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.700
with Russia and it's up to Russia

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.968
how they choose to respond.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:16.769
Something the U.S.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.004
is watching very closely.

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.772
But then he made a distinction here.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.707
An escalation of Russia in Ukraine

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:22.475
is one thing.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.242
The U.S.

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:24.210
has been watching this

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.378
and knows how to handle this,

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:26.712
taking it as it comes

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.246
and keeping an eye

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.214
on the different dynamics

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.282
there in that situation.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:31.651
But escalation outside of Ukraine,

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.252
whether that's in another part of Europe

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.353
against Naito in the Middle East,

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.221
that would put this

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:36.422
in an entirely different

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.357
ballgame completely, he says.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.091
Max

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:40.793
what about tensions between

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:41.861
the US and China?

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:45.932
So we certainly spoke about

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.566
China as well,

00:07:46.566 --> 00:07:47.500
especially days

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.902
after an encounter between the U.S.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:50.903
and the Chinese navies

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.104
at sea in the Taiwan Strait,

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.272
one of the most sensitive areas

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:53.973
for China.

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:54.540
We focused

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.642
on the question of communication.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.411
Where are they on reestablishing

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.346
communications between or at the higher

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:01.581
levels of the military

00:08:01.581 --> 00:08:02.381
is between the U.S.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:03.149
and China.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:03.516
For him,

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.350
he simply stressed

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.886
the need to resume communications

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:07.887
and to keep that going

00:08:07.887 --> 00:08:08.921
because it is

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:10.890
the ability to have dialog, especially,

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.425
especially with tensions high

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.326
as we're seeing them now,

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.794
that makes sure that the relationship

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:16.362
between Beijing and Washington

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:18.197
stays in the realm of competition

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:20.633
and doesn't veer towards conflict Max.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.034
Okay. All right.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.302
Thank you for bringing us that.

